WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:01.840
Tech billionaires wear them,

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:03.240
babies wear them,

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:05.720
even the US vice president is a fan.

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:15.400
Sneakers. Trainers. The tennis shoe.

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:18.080
Whatever you want to call them,
they’re everywhere -

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:21.120
maybe even on your
own feet right now.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:25.080
Tens of billions of pairs are
manufactured every year.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:28.000
The biggest athletic shoe companies
make more in revenue

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:30.560
than the GDP of some countries.

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:33.440
So how did a piece of rubber,
leather and canvas

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:35.440
become such big business?

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:38.480
Let’s go back to the late
19th Century.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:42.880
New sports like croquet and
tennis required new footwear

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:45.480
to protect the grass lawns
they were played on.

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:50.000
Not long after, sneaker
brands started to appear.

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:55.640
Converse’s most famous shoe, the
All-Star, made its debut in 1917.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:00.800
Two of the biggest names in the
sneaker game, Adidas and Puma,

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:02.840
were each founded
by a German brother.

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:05.120
Adi and Rudolf Dassler

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:06.920
got together in the 1920s

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.440
to make athletic shoes.

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:13.400
The Dassler brothers capitalised on
something that’s common sense today.

00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:17.840
If you want people to buy your shoes,
get someone famous to wear them.

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:21.760
That person was
US Olympian Jesse Owens.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:23.720
But Owens, a black athlete,

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:27.040
was set to compete at the
1936 Olympics in Berlin

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:29.400
at a time when Adolf Hitler
and the Nazis

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:32.040
were firmly in control
of Germany.

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:35.920
The Dassler brothers who, along
with many German industrialists,

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:39.680
had joined the Nazi party, took
a risk in approaching Owens.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:44.760
The risk paid off when Owens went on
to win four gold medals.

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:47.000
It was an incredible coup -

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:51.160
a black man upstaging Hitler’s racist
ideology on the world stage.

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:54.640
And he was wearing Dassler shoes.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:00.080
After the war, the brothers split,
each to form their own company -

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:03.440
Adi set up Adidas and Rudi, Puma.

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:06.200
In fact,
Adidas is an amalgamation

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:10.480
of its founder’s first and second
names, Adi and Dassler.

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:15.200
His brother Rudi tried the same
trick, and called his brand 'Ruda'

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:18.680
before realising that
it didn’t roll off the tongue.

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:20.880
But the story of sneakers
is not just about

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:23.120
finding the right name
for your product.

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:25.360
It’s also about marketing.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:32.520
Nike sold huge numbers of shoes
during the jogging boom of the 1970s.

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:34.760
But when they wanted
to move beyond running,

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:37.040
they needed something
extra special.

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:41.040
And they found it in
basketball legend Michael Jordan,

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:44.680
making him the biggest athletic
spokesperson of all time.

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:47.320
The Nike-Jordan partnership
was a huge success

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:52.160
generating more than $100 million
in sales in its first 12 months,

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:56.120
rising to an incredible $3.6 billion,

00:02:56.200 --> 00:03:00.120
or around £2.6 billion,
in revenue in 2020.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:03.160
Nike was also adept at spotting
other opportunities.

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:08.680
Did you know they paid just $35,
or roughly £284, in today's money

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:10.960
for their famous Swoosh logo?

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:13.440
And that the famous Nike slogan
“Just Do it”

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:15.960
was inspired by the
last words, “Let’s Do it”,

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:20.080
of murderer Gary Gilmore
prior to his 1977 execution?

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:22.760
It’s not just athletes -
and death row inmates -

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:24.680
who inspire us to wear sneakers.

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:30.040
In the mid-80s, hip-hop group Run-DMC
signed a landmark deal with Adidas

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:32.920
paving the way for many more
lucractive partnerships

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:35.040
between shoe makers and artists.

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:39.240
Today, Kanye West and Rihanna
each have their own line of sneakers.

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:40.960
And they’re worth big bucks.

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:44.880
West’s collaboration with Adidas,
the Yeezy sneaker line,

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:49.040
was valued at over
£1.2 billion in 2019 .

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:52.960
But what does our appetite for all
these shoes mean for the world?

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:55.720
Environmentally they are
something of a disaster.

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:59.320
A single shoe can contain
65 different parts,

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:01.640
and hundreds of different
processing steps.

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:04.840
As you can imagine,
our shoes stick around in landfills

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:06.920
long after we’ve thrown them away.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:10.680
A rubber sole might take
80 years to biodegrade.

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:13.840
Plastics and synthetics
take hundreds more.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:15.760
Several sneaker companies
are experimenting

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:19.480
with recycled materials and more
sustainable production methods.

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:21.800
But the legacy of our love
affair with sneakers

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:24.720
will be with us for many,
many years to come.

